0..71 Comment "// A native list taken apart by its patterns: `[]`, the elements a list"
72..144 Comment "// pattern writes, a rest `..r` binding the list past them, and `p as x`"
145..224 Comment "// binding the whole value a pattern matches. Each list pattern compiles to the"
225..303 Comment "// list case on the empty list and a cell, so a recursion on the rest descends"
304..364 Comment "// structurally, as a list\'s tail stands one stage below it."
